A rectangular garden uses an existing wall for one side and $64$ m of fencing for the other three sides. Find the dimensions that maximise its area.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-0.4,2)--(4.4,2);
\draw (0,2)--(0,0)--(4,0)--(4,2);
\path (2,2) node[above]{Existing wall};
\path (0,1) node[left]{$x$ m};
\path (4,1) node[right]{$x$ m};
\path (2,0) node[below]{$y$ m};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

An open box is made by cutting squares of side $x$ cm from each corner of a $30$ cm by $12$ cm sheet and folding up the sides. Find the cut size and maximum volume.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=2mm,y=2mm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (30,12);
\draw[dashed] (0,3)--(3,3)--(3,0);
\draw[dashed] (0,9)--(3,9)--(3,12);
\draw[dashed] (27,0)--(27,3)--(30,3);
\draw[dashed] (27,12)--(27,9)--(30,9);
\path (15,12) node[above]{$30$ cm};
\path (30,6) node[right]{$12$ cm};
\path (1.5,0) node[below]{$x$ cm};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A poster has total area $576$ cm$^{2}$ and a $3$ cm margin on every side of its photograph. Find the maximum photograph area.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (4,4);
\draw (0.5,0.5) rectangle (3.5,3.5);
\path (2,0) node[below]{$x$ cm};
\path (4,2) node[right]{$y$ cm};
\draw[<->] (0,2)--(0.5,2);
\path (0.25,2) node[above]{$3$ cm};
\path (2,2) node{Photograph};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A rower is at $P$, $4$ km from the nearest point $A$ on a straight shore. Her destination $B$ is $10$ km along the shore from $A$. She rows at $3$ km/h to $L$, then walks at $5$ km/h to $B$. Find where she should land to minimise her travel time.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=6mm,y=6mm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-0.5,0)--(10.5,0);
\draw (0,0)--(0,4)--(4,0);
\draw (0.3,0)--(0.3,0.3)--(0,0.3);
\path (0,0) node[below left]{$A$};
\path (0,4) node[above]{$P$};
\path (4,0) node[above right]{$L$};
\path (10,0) node[above]{$B$};
\path (0,2) node[left]{$4$ km};
\path (2,0) node[below]{$x$ km};
\path (7,0) node[below]{$10-x$ km};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A line through $P(2,1)$ meets the positive axes at $X(x,0)$ and $Y(0,y)$, where $x>2$. Given $y=\dfrac{x}{x-2}$, find the minimum area of triangle $XOY$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(4.8,0);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,2.8);
\draw (0,2)--(4,0);
\fill (2,1) circle (1.2pt);
\path (0,0) node[below left]{$O$};
\path (4,0) node[below]{$X(x,0)$};
\path (0,2) node[left]{$Y(0,y)$};
\path (2,1) node[above right]{$P(2,1)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
